## Customize flags given to the VM: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here

## Kept small and quiet when idle: the app has few users, and is billed by the
## CPU time and memory it uses (Bunny). By default the VM starts one scheduler
## per core it sees, which on a shared host is the host's cores: each costs
## memory, and wakes up.

## One scheduler, and one dirty CPU scheduler (tantivy's NIFs, Yjs merges)
+S 1:1
+SDcpu 1:1
## Dirty IO schedulers, for SQLite's NIF (default 10)
+SDio 4

## No busy waiting: by default, a scheduler with nothing to do spins for a
## while before sleeping, to react faster to new work
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none

## At most 65536 ports (sockets, files), instead of one per file descriptor
## the host allows: the VM sizes its tables after it, and with Docker's default
## limit (2^31 locally) they took 2 GB of memory
+Q 65536

## Tweak GC to run more often
##-env ERL_FULLSWEEP_AFTER 10

## Enable deployment without epmd
## (requires changing both vm.args and remote.vm.args)
##-start_epmd false -erl_epmd_port 6789
